{"chunk_id": "2f8c25e78249", "text": "Draupadi, living in disguise as Sairindhri during the Pandavas\u2019 incognito year in Virata\u2019s court, pours out her anguish to Bhima. Once a queen served by many, she now grinds sandalwood and obeys Queen Sudeshna, her hands hardened with corns. She laments the cruel reversal of fate that has reduced the mighty Pandavas to servitude and herself to fear and humiliation. Bhima is overcome with grief and rage, cursing his own strength for failing to protect her and recalling how he restrained himself from killing Kichaka when Yudhishthira signaled him to remain silent. To console her, he invokes legendary devoted wives like Sukanya, Sita, Lopamudra, and Savitri, urging patience until the exile ends. Draupadi then reveals Kichaka\u2019s relentless harassment and Sudeshna\u2019s complicity, setting the stage for Bhima\u2019s coming vengeance.\nDraupadi laments her humiliation in Virata\u2019s court; Bhima vows restrained vengeance and urges patience until exile ends while hearing of Kichaka\u2019s harassment.\nThemes: humiliation and exile, suppressed vengeance, marital loyalty, fate and endurance, sexual harassment by power", "vector": [-0.009019363671541214, -0.020361898466944695, 0.00010340026346966624, -0.0017628757050260901, 0.0006918262224644423, 0.0455067902803421, -0.020197909325361252, -0.002685310784727335, -0.005329624284058809, -0.04113376513123512, 0.015756554901599884, 0.0053740376606583595, 0.027891701087355614, 0.003607745748013258, -0.015373916365206242, 0.026019498705863953, 0.04968849569559097, 0.013030247762799263, 0.02834266796708107, -0.03052918054163456, -0.006170065142214298, -0.001964444760233164, 0.006115402095019817, 0.021263834089040756, -0.052284982055425644, 0.01138353068381548, 0.013166905380785465, -0.02828800491988659, 0.010994058102369308, -0.0015510573284700513, -0.024352282285690308, -0.0032063156832009554, 0.0070856669917702675, 0.002171138534322381, -0.032688360661268234, -0.005035811569541